        "identifier": "https://github.com/hkjtsgmc79-boop/colombo-odd-lean/tree/250ff20a0c2edae8f37e5733b439bf9128a877bd",
        "note": "Finite Pfaffian minor-summation infrastructure, with Apache-2.0 attribution retained in source.",
        "relationship": "adapts"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/QuanyuTang/polya-neumann-simply-connected-formalization-Palomar-version-v2/tree/f07f1c7051862ba146429db6eda5dc4e8b020f74",
        "note": "Apache-2.0 local Lipschitz graph definitions and elementary chart lemmas from RequestProject/Defs.lean, BoundaryChart.lean, and JordanWinding.lean are adapted in GinoeClt/Definitions.lean and GinoeClt/Geometry/BoundaryCharts.lean. The chart definition here requires Lipschitz continuity on the chart interval. Only local graph geometry is used; no simple-connectivity hypothesis is imposed on the CLT domain. Attribution is retained in the source headers.",
        "relationship": "adapts"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/human-ai-mathematics/kls-lean/tree/33fff6ea218ae07e42115bd1eacfcf7d39c534cb",
        "note": "Apache-2.0 proof patterns from FunctionalInequalities/Analysis/Graph/{Area,Integral,Divergence}.lean and FunctionalInequalities/KLS/Geometry/Perimeter/{Mollification,MollifiedBoundary}.lean are adapted in GinoeClt/Geometry/{GraphArea,GraphAreaFormula,GraphMeasure, GraphShear,GraphGaussGreen,Mollification,IndicatorApproximation}.lean. The adaptations cover graph area and integration, graph shear and Fubini arguments, compact-support comparisons, indicator convolution estimates, and reflected-test boundary identities. They are specialized to planar Lipschitz graphs with Euclidean one-dimensional Hausdorff measure; the mollification argument uses this project's proved Lipschitz Gauss-Green theorem. Pinned source locations and attribution are retained in the source headers.",
        "relationship": "adapts"
      }
